{
  "_doc": "POST <target.server_url>/api/agent/sdk-credential/grant on the tenant host (section 13.6; internal/orgserver/sdkcred, lane L4). request.body is what setup sends; key_grant is internal/sdkkeygrant/testdata/vectors.json valid[0] (signed by that file's TEST-ONLY key) and redeem_secret is the secret whose hash it carries, so a tenant test that pins the vector key verifies this exact request. responses are what the host answers: minted is sdkcred.GrantRedeemed, which embeds orgcontract.SDKCredentialMinted (the member mint's own body, one owner) and adds dashboard_url and, only when the month's ingest allowance is already used, plan_refusal (the ingest gateway's own 429 body: error, message, quota and the plan detail, from gateway/planrefusal and the meter's decision). Tenant errors are {error: <code>, message: <text>}; key_grant_refused adds reason (a closed vocabulary: internal/sdkkeygrant's Reason values, plus wrong_org, redeem_mismatch, not_a_member, member_inactive). A replaces_key_id that is not this member's key is ignored, never an error (the member mint's named-key rule). Every answer carries Cache-Control: no-store.",
